## 🧠 ML Pipeline — Stage by Stage

### Stage 1 — Pose Extraction
**File:** [`extract_pose.py`](file:///c:/Secure-Eldercare-Project/anomaly-detection/backend/app/ml_services/inference/extract_pose.py)

- Uses **MediaPipe BlazePose** (Google) to detect the human skeleton
- Extracts **33 body landmarks**, each with `[x, y, z, visibility]`
- Returns bounding box `{x, y, w, h}` (normalised 0–1) for canvas drawing
- If no person is detected → returns `pose_valid: false` → pipeline short-circuits

---

### Stage 2 — Feature Engineering (40 Features)
**File:** [`feature_engineer.py`](file:///c:/Secure-Eldercare-Project/anomaly-detection/backend/app/ml_services/inference/feature_engineer.py)

| Feature Group | Indices | Description |
|---|---|---|
| **Joint Angles** | [0–7] | Elbow, shoulder, knee, hip (both sides) — normalised /180 |
| **3D Body Tilt** | [8] | Torso angle from vertical + MediaPipe z-depth enhancement |
| **Slopes** | [9–10] | Hip & shoulder lateral lean |
| **Body Centre** | [11–12] | X, Y position of body's geometric centre |
| **Head Height** | [13] | Nose Y relative to hip centre (standing vs. fallen) |
| **Aspect Ratio** | [14] | `body_h / body_w` — wide = lying, tall = standing |
| **Visibility** | [15–17] | Wrist and average landmark confidence |
| **Velocities** | [18–21] | Body velocity, wrist L/R velocity, head drop speed |
| **Motion Energy** | [22] | Total landmark displacement per frame (Phase 3) |
| **Raw Positions** | [23–38] | Key joint XY for rule engine access |
| **CoM Stability** | [39] | Center of Mass stability score (Phase 3) |

> **Phase 3 Enhancement:** Feature [8] now uses 3D z-depth from MediaPipe for more accurate fall tilt detection. Feature [39] is CoM stability (0=moving, 1=still).

---

### Stage 3 — Sequence Buffer
**File:** [`sequence_buffer.py`](file:///c:/Secure-Eldercare-Project/anomaly-detection/backend/app/ml_services/inference/sequence_buffer.py)

- Maintains a **30-frame rolling window** per person
- Also stores the previous raw frame for velocity computation
- Per-person counter dictionary for fall/aggression/inactivity persistence tracking
- `flush(person_id)` called on WebSocket disconnect to clean memory

---

### Stage 4 — Rule Engine (Always-On)
**File:** [`rule_engine.py`](file:///c:/Secure-Eldercare-Project/anomaly-detection/backend/app/ml_services/inference/rule_engine.py)

Works with zero ML weights — pure geometric heuristics. Priority: **Fall > Aggression > Inactivity**

#### Fall Detection Rules
| Signal | Threshold | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Torso angle | > 45° | Person leaning severely |
| Body centre Y | > 0.65 | Centre of mass dropped low in frame |
| Aspect ratio | < 1.0 | Body wider than tall (horizontal posture) |
| Head drop speed | > threshold | Rapid downward nose movement |
| **Persistence** | ≥ 3 frames | Must confirm across consecutive frames |

#### Aggression Detection Rules
| Signal | Threshold |
|---|---|
| Max wrist velocity | > 0.05/frame |
| Body velocity OR pose energy | above threshold |
| Persistence | ≥ 2 frames |

#### Inactivity Detection Rules
| Duration | Event | Severity |
|---|---|---|
| ≥ 30 sec | `inactivity_warning` | medium |
| ≥ 60 sec | `prolonged_inactivity` | high |
| ≥ 120 sec | `prolonged_inactivity` | critical |

Evidence: `pose_energy < 0.012` sustained for N frames

---

### Stage 5 — ML Models (PyTorch)

#### LSTM Classifier
**File:** [`lstm_model.py`](file:///c:/Secure-Eldercare-Project/anomaly-detection/backend/app/ml_services/models/lstm_model.py)  
**Weights:** [`lstm_weights.pt`](file:///c:/Secure-Eldercare-Project/anomaly-detection/backend/app/ml_services/trained_models/lstm_weights.pt) (893 KB)

- Architecture: `40 → LSTM(128) → LSTM(64) → FC(5)`
- Input: 30-frame × 40-feature sequence
- Output: 5-class probability vector (normal, fall, aggression, inactivity, unusual)
- Threshold: `prob ≥ 0.65` to fire

#### Autoencoder (AE)
**File:** [`autoencoder_model.py`](file:///c:/Secure-Eldercare-Project/anomaly-detection/backend/app/ml_services/models/autoencoder_model.py)  
**Weights:** [`ae_weights.pt`](file:///c:/Secure-Eldercare-Project/anomaly-detection/backend/app/ml_services/trained_models/ae_weights.pt) (2.7 MB)

- Architecture: `40→32→16→8→16→32→40` (encoder + decoder)
- Trained on normal activity sequences only
- Output: **Reconstruction error** (MSE) — high error = anomalous pattern
- Threshold: `ae_error ≥ 0.05` (strict), `≥ 0.10` for standalone detection

> **Training:** Both models trained on a 4-class synthetic dataset (normal, fall, aggression, inactivity) using `train_lstm.py` and `train_ae.py` in the `scripts/` folder.

---

### Stage 6 — Hybrid Decision Fusion
**File:** [`detect_anomaly.py`](file:///c:/Secure-Eldercare-Project/anomaly-detection/backend/app/ml_services/inference/detect_anomaly.py)

Priority cascade:
```
1. LSTM prob ≥ 0.65 AND class != normal  →  LSTM wins
   (confidence boosted +5% if rule engine agrees)
2. Rule engine fired  →  Rule wins
   (confidence boosted +7% if AE also sees anomaly)
3. AE error ≥ 0.10 (2× threshold, rule silent)  →  "unusual_movement"
4. All clear  →  "normal_activity"
```

Source tag in response: `rule_engine` / `lstm` / `lstm+rule` / `rule_engine+ae` / `autoencoder`

---

### Stage 7 — Intelligence Layer (Phase 3)
**File:** [`decision_explainer.py`](file:///c:/Secure-Eldercare-Project/anomaly-detection/backend/app/ml_services/inference/decision_explainer.py)

Every event now includes a full explanation:

```json
{
  "explanation": {
    "reason": "Fall detected: torso tilted 72° from vertical; body centre dropped to 78% of frame; confirmed across 4 frames; LSTM corroborated (p=0.93)",
    "contributing_factors": {
      "torso_tilt_score": 0.91,
      "pose_drop_score": 0.87,
      "horizontal_posture": 0.82,
      "temporal_confirmation": 4,
      "lstm_probability": 0.93,
      "ae_reconstruction_error": 0.047
    },
    "signal_breakdown": {
      "rule_engine": 0.87,
      "temporal": 0.80,
      "lstm": 0.93,
      "autoencoder": 0.72
    }
  }
}
```

Uses sigmoid-scaled factor strengths (0–1) for each contributing signal.

---

### Stage 8 — Prediction Smoothing (Phase 2)
**File:** [`prediction_smoother.py`](file:///c:/Secure-Eldercare-Project/anomaly-detection/backend/app/ml_services/inference/prediction_smoother.py)

- **8-frame rolling majority vote** per person
- Per-class minimum vote requirements (fall=3, inactivity_warning=5)
- Confidence is weighted-average of matching frames (recent frames count more)
- Eliminates single-frame false positives / flickering

---

### Stage 9 — Alert Service (Phase 2)
**File:** [`alert_service.py`](file:///c:/Secure-Eldercare-Project/anomaly-detection/backend/app/services/alert_service.py)

- **8-second cooldown deduplication** per `person_id:event_type` — eliminates spam
- Structured JSON format with `timestamp`, `confidence`, `evidence`, `session_id`
- **3 persistence layers:** MongoDB `anomaly_alerts` + `anomaly_logs`, in-memory ring buffer (200 alerts), session JSONL file (`logs/session_alerts.jsonl`)
- Console dispatch for `critical`/`high` severity with full alert details

