## 🎓 Viva Talking Points

### "How does your system detect a fall?"
> "When a frame arrives, MediaPipe extracts 33 body landmarks. We compute a 40-dimensional feature vector including the 3D body tilt angle, head drop speed, and aspect ratio. If the torso angle exceeds 45°, the body centre is low in frame, and this persists for 3 or more consecutive frames, the rule engine fires `fall_detected`. This is then confirmed by the LSTM classifier which independently analyses the full 30-frame sequence and outputs a probability. If both agree, confidence is boosted. Finally, our 8-frame majority vote smoother prevents single-frame false positives."

### "What makes it more than just rule-based?"
> "We have 3 detection layers. The rule engine always runs with zero latency. The LSTM sees the temporal sequence of 30 frames and can detect patterns the rules miss. The Autoencoder is trained only on normal activity — if the reconstruction error spikes, it flags unusual movement that even the rule engine would miss. The decision fusion layer combines all three with source tagging."

### "Why did you add the Intelligence Layer?"
> "Every anomaly now includes a plain-English reason explaining which signals triggered it — torso angle, velocity, temporal confirmation count. This makes the system auditable and trustworthy, which is essential in a healthcare context. Caregivers can see exactly why an alert fired."

### "How do you handle false positives?"
> "Three mechanisms: (1) The rule engine requires events to persist across multiple frames before firing. (2) The prediction smoother requires a majority vote across 8 frames. (3) The alert service has an 8-second cooldown per patient-event pair, so repeated triggers during the same event are deduplicated."

### "Can you demonstrate fall detection live?"
> "Yes — I can use the Scenario Mode. The system provides four demo simulation buttons. Pressing Fall injects a fully-formed synthetic event with a fallen-body skeleton rendered on the canvas, complete with explaining factors, confidence score, and event timeline entry. This allows safe, repeatable demonstrations."

